{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Despicable Me Minion Mayhem is a 4-D computer-animated simulator ride attraction located at Universal Studios Florida, Universal Studios Hollywood, and Universal Studios Japan.","title":"Despicable Me Minion Mayhem"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The attraction is based on Universal Studios and Illumination Entertainment's 2010 animated film "Despicable Me" and its franchise and employs the use of 3-D HD digital animation.","title":"Despicable Me Minion Mayhem"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The attraction replaced Jimmy Neutron's Nicktoon Blast (Before Jimmy Neutron's Nicktoon Blast, that space was The Funtastic World of Hanna-Barbera) in Florida, in Hollywood, and in Japan.","title":"Despicable Me Minion Mayhem"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon is an American late-night talk show hosted by Jimmy Fallon, on NBC.","title":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The show premiered on February 17, 2014, and is produced by Broadway Video and Universal Television.","title":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is the seventh incarnation of NBC's long-running "Tonight Show" franchise, with Fallon serving as the sixth host.","title":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The show also stars sidekick and announcer Steve Higgins and house band The Roots.","title":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "The Tonight Show" is produced by Katie Hockmeyer and executive-produced by Lorne Michaels.","title":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The show records from Studio 6B in Rockefeller Center, New York City.","title":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" This was the first version of "The Tonight Show" filmed in New York City since "The Tonight Show Starring Johnny Carson" in 1972.","title":"The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Twister...Ride It Out was a special effects attraction located at Universal Studios Florida, based on the 1996 film "Twister".","title":"Twister...Ride it Out"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was announced in 1997 and replaced the Ghostbusters Spooktacular attraction in the New York area of the park.","title":"Twister...Ride it Out"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The attraction was hosted by actors Bill Paxton and Helen Hunt, who starred in the original film.","title":"Twister...Ride it Out"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The attraction closed on November 2, 2015 and replaced with "Race Through New York Starring Jimmy Fallon", which opened on April 6, 2017.","title":"Twister...Ride it Out"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Backdraft is a fire special effects show at Universal Studios Japan, and formerly Universal Studios Hollywood theme park.","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The show is based on the film of the same name.","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Visitors can learn how the pyrotechnic effects were created and experience some of them first hand.","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The Hollywood attraction was supposed to officially close after Labor Day 2009 to be replaced by in 2011 but remained open to appease the temporary closures of other attractions for annual refurbishment.","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The Hollywood attraction officially closed on April 11, 2010.","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The attraction remains part of the Osaka park.","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" A similar styled show demonstrating storm effects, Lights!","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Camera!","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" Action!","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" Hosted by Steven Spielberg, opened in Universal Studios Singapore in 2010.","title":"Backdraft (attraction)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Jaws is a theme park attraction at Universal Studios Japan.","title":"Jaws (ride)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Based upon the films of the same name.","title":"Jaws (ride)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The attraction places guests aboard tour boats for what should be a leisurely tour of Amity Harbor, but instead becomes a harrowing chase between the craft and a very determined great white shark.","title":"Jaws (ride)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Jaws is an expanded version of a famous scene on the long-running backlot tour at Universal Studios Hollywood, also inspired by the film, and can be found at Universal Studios Japan near Osaka, and formerly, at Universal Studios Florida in Orlando.","title":"Jaws (ride)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Waterworld: A Live Sea War Spectacular is an attraction based on the 1995 film "Waterworld" found at Universal Studios Hollywood (1995), Universal Studios Japan (2001), and Universal Studios Singapore (2010).","title":"Waterworld: A Live Sea War Spectacular"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The original attraction opened at the same time as the film.","title":"Waterworld: A Live Sea War Spectacular"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Although the film was considered a critical and financial disappointment, the show was highly praised, winning a 1996 Thea Award from the Themed Entertainment Association.","title":"Waterworld: A Live Sea War Spectacular"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The attraction remains highly rated by park guests.","title":"Waterworld: A Live Sea War Spectacular"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Ghostbusters
